WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.380
Black Mirror Season 5 is here with a stack
of easter eggs and shared universe connections

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.800
to many previous episodes including San Junipero,
15 Million Merits, Bandersnatch, and White

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.800
Christmas.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.750
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm revealing all the crucial details you

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.400
might have missed in the fifth season and
my theory on how all the episodes connect

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.400
together.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.599
Obviously, Black Mirror spoilers ahead so
take care.

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:27.970
The Striking Vipers episode examines what
happens when two old college friends Danny

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.449
and Karl reconnect later in life.

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.430
When Karl buys Danny the new Striking Vipers
X video game, as Danny goes to open the box

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.269
with the VR add-on we can see that it's manufactured
by TCKR Systems.

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:46.320
TCKR is the neural technology company responsible
for the simulated reality tech in San Junipero

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.660
and is also the company which conducted medical
experiments out of St Juniper's Hospital in

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.690
the "Black Museum" episode.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.760
The way that the Striking Vipers X game emulates
physical sensations means it could also be

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:03.410
linked to another piece of TCKR tech, the
Symphatic Diagnoser that Dr Peter Dawson used

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.950
to experience his subjects' pain and pleasure
in "Black Museum".

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.730
"Turns out, we haven't discovered how to share
knowledge..."

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.120
"But physical sensations."

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.120
"Bingo."

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.150
Now, even though Karl and Danny experience
the pain from the sensations in the game,

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.960
there isn't any lasting physical effect on
them or their game characters.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.510
"Don't worry, it resets.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.690
No harm done."

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.130
It's very similar to how whoever wears the
Symphatic Diagnoser doesn't suffer any lasting

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:32.630
injury either:
"And even nutsier s-, Hector felt the burn,

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.341
but took no damage at all.

00:01:34.341 --> 00:01:37.320
All of the experience, none of the physical
cost."

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.980
And there's even a parallel to how Karl feels
as a woman when he's in the game with how

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:45.660
Dr Lawson experienced both male and female
orgasms when he used the Symphatic Diagnoser

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:46.660
with his girlfriend.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.660
"How does it feel?

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.040
Being in a woman's body?"

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:55.170
"Like, one's a guitar solo, the other's a
whole f- orchestra."

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.720
The Striking Vipers game also gets referenced
in the "Rachel, Jack and Ashley Too" episode

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.120
of season 5.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.470
During a news report about Ashley O's coma,
a ticker on screen mentions that SaitoGemu's

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.930
shares have jumped after the release of Striking
Vipers.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:14.360
SaitoGemu is the company first seen in the
"Playtest" episode which hired Cooper Redfield

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.930
as a video game tester, and their work on
augmented reality games ties back clearly

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.400
to Striking Vipers X.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.140
"What we're working on is an interactive augmented
reality system."

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.190
"Like VR?"

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.300
"More like layers on top of reality."

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:33.030
The little round headpiece that Danny and
Karl wear to play Striking Vipers isn't totally

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.390
dissimilar to the mushroom SaitoGemu implanted
in Cooper either.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:41.880
That mushroom malfunctioned though leading
to Cooper's death and it looks like that tech

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.930
from Playtest may have been replaced with
the little button that Danny and Karl use

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.540
in Striking Vipers.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.870
That little disc made by TCKR for Striking
Vipers X may also be a version of the devices

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.010
used in San Junipero.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.319
And the way Striking Vipers X brings old friends
Danny and Karl back together in an unconventional

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:06.530
way may also fulfil the Edge magazine headline
in "Playtest" that TCKR would turn nostalgia

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.210
into a game.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:13.110
It's a humorous moment when the Ashley Too
doll has her four percent brain limiter erased

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:17.319
and the full unfiltered consciousness of Ashely
O is unleashed.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:22.610
We next learn that the little doll actually
has an entire digital copy of Ashley's mind.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:27.510
This isn't the first time we've seen consciousness
replicated on Black Mirror, and Ashley Too

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:32.000
may be an early form of the cookie technology
we see in White Christmas where Greta has

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.069
her mind copied into a cookie so that it can
perform her household chores.

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.940
In fact, the robot believes she's a real version
of Ashley much like Greta's cookie did too.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.010
"So, you're really Ashley O?"

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.960
"Oh, yeah, of course I am."

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:46.960
"Really, really?"

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.160
"Well, OK, a synaptic snapshot of me, if you
wanna get technical about it."

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.910
The way Ashley argues over whether Ashley
Too is really an individual character is an

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:00.540
early indicator of how cookies in other Black
Mirror episodes are treated as slaves without

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.230
any rights and are even horrendously tortured.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:07.709
"Most people would say,
'She's only made of code, she's not real.'

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:08.709
F- her."

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:10.349
"I can't believe there's two of you."

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.880
"That thing isn't all of me.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:13.880
I'm all of me."

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.650
That issue was later addressed in the "Hated
in the Nation" episode where a news ticker

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.930
announced that cookies have been declared
to have human rights.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.370
The drugs that Ashley O's aunt and managers
give her to keep her docile and stop her from

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.509
acting up could be what's in the Cuppliance
drink that the contestants on "Hot Shots"

00:04:30.509 --> 00:04:34.889
in the "15 Million Merits" episode are made
to drink before going on stage.

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:35.889
"Cuppliance?

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:36.889
No, thanks.

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:37.889
A-ha.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:38.889
Yes, thanks!

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:40.199
It's compulsory for all contestants."

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:44.590
And Abi's Khan's song "Anyone Who Knows What
Love Is" which she sings on Hot Shots pops

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.240
up during the exclusive report on Ashley O
to demonstrate how her aunt and managers are

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.879
using voice mimicry software to vocalise Ashley's
voice recordings into brand new songs.

00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:59.800
And after Ashley is deliberately poisoned
by her aunt, USN reports that she's been rushed

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.009
to St Juniper's ICU.

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:04.860
St Juniper's has come up a few times in Black
Mirror.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.409
It's the hospital from "Black Museum" where
Rolo Haynes used to work.

00:05:08.409 --> 00:05:14.060
And in Bandersnatch, Stefan visits a different
Dr Haynes at the St Juniper's Medical Facility.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.819
The name St Juniper also likely links back
to the fan favourite episode San Junipero

00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:23.219
which, fittingly for Ashley's story, features
people who are dead in the real world while

00:05:23.219 --> 00:05:25.969
they're alive in their own virtual reality.

00:05:25.969 --> 00:05:31.809
Earlier in the episode, an eerily familiar
ad plays on the TV in Rachel and Jack's bedroom:

00:05:31.809 --> 00:05:33.039
"Live.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:34.259
Breathe.

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:35.490
Smell."

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.710
"Live.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.940
Breathe.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.169
Smell."

00:05:39.169 --> 00:05:43.490
Willow Grain were the manufacturers of the
memory recording neural implants that featured

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:48.430
in "The Entire History of You" and which allowed
people to replay memories either on screens

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.729
or in front of their own eyes.

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:50.889
"Because memory is for living."

00:05:50.889 --> 00:05:54.189
"Because memory is for living."

00:05:54.189 --> 00:06:00.029
After the ad, the Funtertainment Daily show
comes on and the host mentions a Sea of Tranquility

00:06:00.029 --> 00:06:01.029
reboot.

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:05.509
"Sea of Tranquility" is the Black Mirror universe
HBO show that was mentioned in the very first

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:09.810
episode of the series "The National Anthem":
"Noel won an Emmy by his effects work on that

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.159
HBO moon Western thing."

00:06:12.159 --> 00:06:13.680
"Sea Of Tranquillity."

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:19.460
And cosplayer fans of that TV show also appeared
in the "Nosedive" episode of season 3.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:24.740
The Funtertainment presenter also talks about
Tusk making a "boo boo" on a British TV show

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:29.979
and a scene taken directly from the "Hated
In The Nation" episode appears on the TV screen.

00:06:29.979 --> 00:06:34.999
In that scene, the rapper Tusk went on a rant
and insulted a young fan of his on the programme.

00:06:34.999 --> 00:06:38.990
And this news report suggests that both Black
Mirror episodes probably take place around

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.529
the same time.

00:06:40.529 --> 00:06:45.860
The USN news tickers in the Ashley Too episode
also help establish where the events may occur

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.779
in relation to other Black Mirror episodes.

00:06:47.779 --> 00:06:53.479
For example, one headline reads "museum owner's
body found in smoking ruins" referring to

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:58.520
the end of the "Black Museum" episode where
Rolo Haynes and his museum are burned down.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:02.940
Another ticker announces an architect has
been "arrested on multiple murder charges".

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.330
This likely relates to Mia Nolan, the architect
from the "Crocodile" episode who was about

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.740
to be apprehended by police at the end of
that story.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:15.270
Colin Ritman, the game programmer played by
Will Poulter in Bandersnatch, also gets a

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.560
shout-out in the name of Rachel's school "Ritman
High".

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:23.060
As for Smithereens, well, it's absolutely
loaded with easter eggs and references to

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.949
other Black Mirror episodes.

00:07:24.949 --> 00:07:30.050
If we examine the rideshare app's map on Chris's
phone more closely, we can see that the Smithereen

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:35.930
UK office is located near Fence's Pizza which
previously appeared in the episodes "USS Callister"

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.930
and "Crocodile".

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.860
"Welcome to Fence's Pizza.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.490
Your pizza is ready for collection."

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:46.809
And there's an empty Fence's pizza box at
Chris's house when the police visit to investigate.

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:51.800
Back on the map of locations, near Smithereen's
UK office is the Medina Plaza Hotel, which

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.909
is where a Fence's Pizza driverless vehicle
was involved in an accident in the "Crocodile"

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:57.909
episode.

00:07:57.909 --> 00:08:02.360
Black Mirror's bank, National Allied, also
has a branch nearby and the bank has appeared

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.220
previously in both "Shut Up and Dance" and
"Playtest".

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:10.580
And, appropriately enough, the video game
company SaitoGemu has an arcade nearby.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:15.389
Other location easter eggs in the area include
Blestow Park, a reference to actress Alice

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:18.460
Eve's character Naomi Blestow from "Nosedive";

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:23.059
Redfield Theatre, a nod to actor Wyatt Russell's
character Cooper Redfield from "Playtest".

00:08:23.059 --> 00:08:28.460
There's a Dawson Burger Bar, a reference to
Dr Peter Dawson from "Black Museum";

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.020
Numerous characters from "Men Against Fire"
also get a shout-out.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:37.169
There's Atelier Arquette, a nod to the antagonist
Arquette, who's played by actor Michael Kelly.

00:08:37.169 --> 00:08:41.399
Stripe's Cocktail Bar references actor Malachi
Kirby's character Stripe.

00:08:41.399 --> 00:08:47.420
And Raiman's tips its hat to actress Madeline
Brewer's character Raiman, aka Hunter.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.490
The street outside Smithereen's office is
called Skillane Street, an easter egg to Victoria

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.560
Skillane from the "White Bear" episode.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:58.800
Opposite the office is the Bandersnatch Theatre,
a hat-tip to the interactive choose-your-own-adventure

00:08:58.800 --> 00:08:59.800
episode.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.010
And Smithereen was itself referenced in the
"Pearl Ritman" ending to Bandersnatch, where

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:09.410
a UKN news ticker stated that a Senate Committee
was grilling Bauer over Russian bots.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:14.850
This ticker also refers to real-life events
in 2018 where the heads of social media companies

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:20.009
testified before the US senate about Russian
interference in US elections and the fake

00:09:20.009 --> 00:09:23.130
accounts being created on these platforms.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:27.509
And although Billy Bauer, the head of Smithereen,
isn't supposed to be based on any specific

00:09:27.509 --> 00:09:32.459
real-life person, Charlie Brooker, the creator
of Black Mirror, told EW that he thought it

00:09:32.459 --> 00:09:37.250
was interesting that last year Jack Dorsey,
the CEO of Twitter had tweeted he'd gone "on

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.870
a 10-day silent retreat."

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:44.589
Inside the Smithereen UK office is a huge
screen packed with headlines and hashtags

00:09:44.589 --> 00:09:48.430
referencing numerous other Black Mirror episodes
and moments.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:53.019
First up, there's a headline that Prime Minister
Callow is meeting with EU negotiators, and

00:09:53.019 --> 00:09:58.339
on the hashtag wall there's some related trending
topics such as #oinkoinkcallow referring to

00:09:58.339 --> 00:10:02.740
"The National Anthem" episode where the PM
Michael Callow was blackmailed into having

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.470
sex with a pig.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:08.720
Related to that is the snoutrage hashtag which
refers to the uncannily similar real-life

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:13.500
allegation that the former British Prime Minister
David Cameron placed a "private part of his

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.759
anatomy" into the mouth of a dead pig during
an initiation ceremony for an Oxford University

00:10:17.759 --> 00:10:19.830
dining society.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:23.880
Snoutrage was one of the hashtags among others
which trended on Twitter when the allegation

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.910
became public.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.720
The SaitoGemu trending hashtags may refer
to the company's release of Striking Vipers

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:34.449
or it could suggest a collaboration with Netflix
which was hinted at in the "Pearl Ritman"

00:10:34.449 --> 00:10:36.230
ending to Bandersnatch.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:41.279
#AshleyOWembley obviously refers to Miley
Cyrus's character Ashley O who's probably

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:44.600
playing a concert at Wembley at the time of
this episode.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:49.879
And #SeaofTranquilityReboot relates to that
entertainment news announcement in the "Rachel,

00:10:49.879 --> 00:10:51.899
Jack and Ashley Too" episode.

00:10:51.899 --> 00:10:56.740
#Tucker is also trending which could have
multiple meanings in the Black Mirror universe.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:02.160
There's Tucker's bar from San Junipero;
the software company Tuckersoft from Bandersnatch;

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:07.370
and Tucker may also be a popular way of reading
the acronym for TCKR Systems.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:11.079
#StJunipersStrike is another St Juniper's
reference.

00:11:11.079 --> 00:11:15.310
And the other two hashtags are BargainHunt
and gogglebox which, for any non-Brits watching

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:19.569
this video, are two real-life British reality
TV shows.

00:11:19.569 --> 00:11:23.870
After Chris demands to speak to Billy Bauer,
one of the Smithereen managers in London goes

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.519
to call the US office, and as she scrolls
through her phone it reveals a huge list of

00:11:28.519 --> 00:11:30.050
other Black Mirror characters.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:34.899
A few that I spotted are Bing from "Fifteen
Million Merits", Cooper from "Playtest", Dudani

00:11:34.899 --> 00:11:40.240
from USS Callister, Greta from White Christmas,
Hector from "Shut Up and Dance", Lacie from

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:43.972
"Nosedive", Liam from "The Entire History
of You", and Nish from "Black Museum".

00:11:43.972 --> 00:11:44.972
There's a lot more to discover and the phone
basically looks like the IMDB page for the

00:11:44.972 --> 00:11:45.972
whole Black Mirror series!

00:11:45.972 --> 00:11:49.620
And there's a fun little meta easter egg when
the phone call is patched through and Smithereen's

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:56.230
US HQ is revealed to be in Los Gatos, California,
which is also the location of Netflix's headquarters.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:01.740
So, did you spot any other interesting details,
easter eggs or connections in the new season

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.740
of Black Mirror?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.350
And which was your favourite episode in season
five?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.500
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:12.069
For another shared universe video, tap left
to learn exactly how Jordan Peele's Us and

00:12:12.069 --> 00:12:16.519
Get Out movies are connected or tap right
for another video you're sure to like.

00:12:16.519 --> 00:12:18.730
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:19.839
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

